CHAPTER.VERS:
He returns to the proposition of the second verse, first warning the hearers, that from now on they do not esteem as lords those whom God has appointed to be ministers and not lords of their salvation. This is done by those that depend upon men, and not upon God that speaks by them. Therefore let no man
Please himself. glory in men. For all things are
Helps, appointed for your benefit. yours;

